# /review-code

Run the review-code skill to perform a critical, evidence-based code review before creating a PR.

**What it does:**
- Gets the diff (uncommitted changes or vs a branch)
- Reviews for bugs, security issues, design problems, style issues
- Groups findings by severity (Critical, Important, Minor, Nitpick)
- Provides file:line references and suggested fixes
- Detects deliberate vs accidental changes to avoid false positives
- Checks git history for regression risks

**Modes:**
- **default (1 agent):** Standard review - fast, thorough, cost-effective
- **full (2 agents):** Adds context analysis (git history, architecture)
- **paranoid (3 agents):** Maximum scrutiny (bugs + design + history agents)

**Usage:**
```
/review-code                  # Uncommitted changes, 1 agent
/review-code main             # Diff against main, 1 agent
/review-code abc123f          # Diff against commit hash, 1 agent
/review-code full             # Uncommitted changes, 2 agents
/review-code main full        # Diff against main, 2 agents
/review-code paranoid         # Uncommitted changes, 3 agents
/review-code main paranoid    # Diff against main, 3 agents
/review-code help             # Show help
```

**Output:**
- Findings grouped by severity (Critical, Important, Minor, Nitpick)
- Summary and recommendation (Ready to PR / Fix issues first / Needs rework)

